  "setup": "Requires one Intel Arc Pro B70 32 GB, 25 GB of free host RAM, and 131 GB on a local NVMe SSD: 85.14 GB of weights plus the 45.8 GB packed expert store that the image's pack-store step builds once (prepare). Routed experts stay on NVMe behind the VRAM expert cache (8,000 slots) and a 8 GB RAM tier; a decode pick that is in neither is read from NVMe while the MoE kernel waits (exact decode miss path, EXL3_EXACT_MISS), so no expert pick is ever masked; VRAM evictions are not written back (EXL3_NVTIER_NO_VICTIM). The n-gram (engram) table is read from NVMe. NEXTN MTP 3 steps / 4 draft tokens (the MTP layer's 512 experts stay pinned in the RAM tier). Context 262,144 tokens with a 270,336-token fp8 KV cache; vision (images). Measured on omarchy (EPYC 7443P, PCIe 4.0 x16, md RAID0 of 4x Samsung 9100 PRO, xfs): container-held RAM (anon + shmem PSS) peak 24.4 GB while serving; local-ai-recipe-kit sweep prefill 1,056-1,076 tok/s from 8K to 64K, decode 32.9-33.3 tok/s aggregate at 1-4 users, C1 at 32K 35.4; reference panel top-1 0.9887, KL 0.00121; needle 233,529 tokens pass. The container limit leaves headroom for the shutdown path.",
